proof.text:
Treat first the normalization $
u:\widetilde D	o D$. By [lem-per-prime-power-costalk-reduction], it is finite, a universal homeomorphism, unchanged at the generic point, and $\widetilde D$ is an excellent strictly henselian trait. Its closed residue degree $d$ is purely inseparable and invertible in $\Lambda$. The etale equivalence identifies $
u^!$ with $
u^*$, using the adjunction counit, and identifies their supported restrictions. Under this equivalence, the counit-defined tensor map is the identity tensor comparison. By the finite purely inseparable field clause of [lem-per-prime-power-regular-gysin], $B_{
u, ar\eta,L}=1$ and $B_{
u, ar s,L}=d\cdot1$ in these identifications. Definition [def-per-potential-dualizing-complex] gives $\operatorname{sp}_D(L)=d^{-1}\operatorname{sp}_{\widetilde D}(
u^*L)$. Consequently the two paths are equal:
$$B_{
u, ar s,L}(1)[2]\operatorname{sp}_D(L)=d\,d^{-1}\operatorname{sp}_{\widetilde D}(
u^*L)=\operatorname{sp}_{\widetilde D}(
u^!L)B_{
u, ar\eta,L}.$$
This proves the normalization case, for all degrees and arbitrary $L$.
